From 3cffb479b0d470863439be809c86d5b3687c6055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pascal Paillet <p.paillet@st.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Apr 2024 17:15:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 618/841] feat(st-pmic): add support for STPMIC1L and STPMIC2L

Add the support for STPMIC1L and STPMIC2L.
- The BUCK1 can support an high voltage range like BUCK2 depending
on the NVM content.
- Those PMIC support GPO that are used to control external regulators.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git f428c3905924e4ff42a06b4dc864cd1dbb3b7e0f feat(st-pmic): add support for STPMIC1L and STPMIC2L]
Change-Id: I0ccd6aa0768873f8fc94fd514ddf70788ceea4bb
Signed-off-by: Pascal Paillet <p.paillet@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/378255
Reviewed-by: Pascal PAILLET <p.paillet@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
